All clean. Here's what the fix was:

**Root cause:** The undo_last_commit_in_real_repo test in commands_git.rs changes the process CWD using a local CWD_MUTEX, while the new commands_goal.rs tests also change CWD but use #[serial] from serial_test. These two synchronization mechanisms don't coordinate with each other, so the tests could run concurrently and interfere with each other's CWD — causing the git test to execute in the wrong directory.

Fix: Added use serial_test::serial; to the `commands_git::tests module and #[serial] to the undo_last_commit_in_real_repo` test. This ensures it never runs concurrently with the goal tests (or any other #[serial] tests that change CWD).

